o its containment it exhibited extreme  aggression towards humans and attempted  to convert them into instances of  scp-778 1 whenever possible  this behavior led to it to actively seek  human population centers though it chose  only such places which allowed it to act  covertly from information gathered in  conversations with SCP 1770 and  observations of field agents involved in  its capture it has been deduced that the  process of converting humans served as a  sort of artistic outlet for SCP 17:70  and that it was compelled to perform it  possibly by an external force see  interview long since its containment the  subject showed no signs of this  compulsion and all attempts at  conversion on its part ceased even when  granted a helpless subject for the  process  addendum 1770 the following our  interviews made with SCP 1770 during  various stages of its containment  interview log 1771 interviewer dr.  interviewed SCP 1774 word this interview  was made immediately following SCP 1770s  capture at this stage no artistic  stimulus was required playing  [Music]  interview log 1775 interviewer dr.  interviewed as CP 1774 word this  interview with s CP 1770 was made in one  of its more lucid moments when it was  fairly responsive and coherent subject  was shown a copy of Monet's water lilies  as a stimulus  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  closing statement it appears SCP 17:70  believes it has lost its ability to bind  with humans and indeed it's motivation  to do so nevertheless considering the  potential risks it still holds current  security measures are to be maintained  recommending further investigation of  the force SCP 17:70 mentioned  [Music]  okay I feel like I have to apologize my  voice is very tired at the moment I  think I'm sick or rundown or something  even more so than usual so I can only  apologize anyway I think that about does  it for today thank you all for listening  if indeed you still are and you are all  dismissed  good bye  I would like to